On the same day, 215 Canadians (176 people from the first aircraft, and 39 of the second aircraft leased by the U.S. government) were evacuated from Wuhan to CFB Trenton for two weeks.
On 11 February, another aircraft carrying 185 Canadians from Wuhan landed at CFB Trenton.
Australian authorities evacuated 277 people on February 3 and 4 to Christmas Island Detention Centre, which has been replaced as a quarantine facility, where they stay for 14 days.
New Zealand evacuation aircraft arrived in Auckland on 5 February; its passengers (including several people from Australia and the Pacific) were quarantined at a naval base in Whangaparoa, north of Aukland.
On February 15, the United States announced that it would move Americans to the Diamond Princess cruise ship.
On February 21, an aircraft carrying 129 Canadians who had been evacuated from Diamond Princess landed in Trento, Ontario.
