Health screening was carried out prior to emissions, and four South Africans who showed signs of the coronavirus had been abandoned to reduce the risk.
Only South Africans have tested were negative.
The test results ensure that all South Africans, including aviation crews, pilots, hotel workers, police and soldiers involved in the humanitarian mission, as a precaution, were all placed under surveillance and quarantined for 14 days at The Ranch Resort.
In March, the U.S. began withdrawing some of its troops from Iraq due to the pandemic.
On 5 February, China's Foreign Minister stated that 21 countries (including Belarus, Pakistan, Trinidad and Tobago, Egypt and Iran) had sent aid to China.
Several Chinese students at American universities have joined forces to help send aid to virus-hit areas in China, along with a joint group in the larger Chicago area, has reportedly successfully delivered 50,000 N95 face masks to a hospital in Hubei province on January ’ 30.
On February 5, Bill and Melinda Gates announced a $100-million donation to the WHO to fund vaccine research and co-treatment efforts to protect "risky populations in Africa and South Asia".
